{#- The GOV.UK tree's layout (ADR-152 decisions 6, 7 and 13; slice GR2a). The frame a page of this tree stands in, kept to what the
    specification names: a skip link first, a banner landmark holding the product's name and the sign-out form, the page's own content
    in the one main landmark, and the page's data block and scripts. There is no script or style in it, no footer and no
    GOV.UK identity: the crown, the GOV.UK logotype and the GOV.UK typeface are shown only with `appearance.govuk_identity` on and on a
    gov.uk address (decision 14), a switch this tree does not have yet, so none of them is here. The stylesheet is `packages/design`'s, built,
    as the Default tree's is, until the GOV.UK tree has stylesheets of its own (it will use govuk-frontend's macros and styles when a
    page first needs them; the package is in the licence register, and is not a dependency of this service yet). -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-GB" data-tree="govuk">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
{% if csrfToken %}<meta name="csrf-token" content="{{ csrfToken }}">{% endif %}
<title>{% block title %}{{ title }}{% endblock %} · OspreyFlow</title>
{% if stylesheet %}<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ stylesheet }}">{% endif %}
</head>
<body>
<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to main content</a>
<header class="app-header">
<span class="brand-mark__name">OspreyFlow</span>
{% if csrfToken %}<div class="app-header__account"><form method="post" action="/session/sign-out">
<input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
<button type="submit" class="btn">Sign out</button>
</form></div>
{% endif %}</header>
<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
{% block content %}{% endblock %}
</main>
{#- The data block a page's interactive module reads (ADR-152 decision 1). It is data, not code: nothing here needs a script to run. -#}
{% block page_data %}<script type="application/json" id="page-data" nonce="{{ cspNonce }}">{"page":"{{ page }}"}</script>{% endblock %}
{#- A page's modules go here, each a script element whose src is asset('modules/NAME.ts'), a file the build made. Never inline code. -#}
{% block scripts %}{% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
